   "plan": ".claude/plans/space_membership_covector_gauge.md (unit U2c)",
   "cause": "The integrated reaction rate became the co-vector pairing <flat(sigma), phi> = sum over (g, i) of (sigma_gi dV_i) phi_gi, one sum over the whole array, where it was sum_i V_i (sum_g sigma_gi phi_gi); the diffusion and homogeneous <1, .> became flat(unit). The same integral, re-associated: every k-quotient the outer iteration evaluates moves by at most 3 ULP on identical flux, and the eigenvalue iteration, whose stopping tolerance is far coarser than one ULP, carries that to at most 18 ULP at the converged k.",
   "criteria": {
    "principled_form": "the reaction rate is the canonical pairing of the co-vector V.flat(sigma) with the flux (the metric read once, at the mint)",
